# Every file checks out with LF on every platform. The repo is already all-LF,
# so this changes nothing today; it keeps that true on machines we do not own.
# Without it, Git rewrites line endings on Windows checkouts, which silently
# changes the bytes of any file pinned by hash.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The vendored ponytail snapshot is pinned by SHA-256 in PROVENANCE.md and
# checked by tests/test_repository.py. Git's automatic line-ending translation
# rewrites the bytes on Windows checkouts (LF -> CRLF), so the hash can never
# match there. Marking these paths as non-text disables that translation and
# keeps the snapshot verbatim on every platform, which is the whole point of
# vendoring it.
skills/ponytail/** -text
